WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.440
For every actor who reverts back to their
usual self the second they hear the word "cut,"

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.660
there's another who stays in character for
the entire duration of a film's production.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:13.350
Of course, living in character around the
clock can lead to some pretty unusual situations

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:17.680
— as proven by these hilarious things actors
did while in character.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.359
Wesley Snipes left Post-It notes as Blade

00:00:20.359 --> 00:00:25.390
Blade: Trinity director David S. Goyer and
star Wesley Snipes had an infamous on-set

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:30.460
battle over Snipes' refusal to take direction
as a leather-wearing vampire hunting ninja.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:34.190
The whole thing culminated in an argument
that turned physical when Snipes attempted

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:36.359
to throttle Goyer with his bare hands.

00:00:36.359 --> 00:00:41.069
From that point on, Snipes refused to speak
to Goyer for the rest of the shoot.

00:00:41.069 --> 00:00:45.199
According to co-star Patton Oswalt, Snipes
communicated solely with the director via

00:00:45.199 --> 00:00:46.199
Post-It notes.

00:00:46.199 --> 00:00:52.030
As an added bonus, they were allegedly all
written in character, each signed "From Blade."

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:54.569
Leonard Nimoy groks Spock

00:00:54.569 --> 00:00:58.719
Because of his high intelligence, the Star
Trek character Spock was extraordinarily popular

00:00:58.719 --> 00:01:03.329
with career academics and scientists, many
of whom saw the character as a peer.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:07.799
As a result, Spock actor Leonard Nimoy was
often invited to sit in on lectures — and

00:01:07.799 --> 00:01:12.689
even look over theses and research proposals
by fans who assumed he had a similar knowledge

00:01:12.689 --> 00:01:14.439
of the fields of science.

00:01:14.439 --> 00:01:18.170
To spare the feelings of people who couldn't
tell the difference between an actor and a

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:22.960
pointy-eared alien from the future, Nimoy
would affect Spock's mannerisms and tell people,

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:26.500
"Well, it certainly looks like you're headed
in the right direction" — regardless of

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.390
whether he actually understood anything they'd
said.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.810
"Fascinating."

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:34.329
Robert Downey Jr.: Method Man

00:01:34.329 --> 00:01:39.109
In Tropic Thunder, Robert Downey Jr.'s Kirk
Lazarus is supposedly one of the world's most

00:01:39.109 --> 00:01:43.399
gifted Method actors — and so committed
to his craft that he undergoes surgery to

00:01:43.399 --> 00:01:47.960
change the pigmentation of his skin in order
to appear black while portraying his character

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.249
Lincoln Osiris.

00:01:49.249 --> 00:01:54.140
Fittingly, Downey stayed in character as Osiris
throughout the DVD commentary for the film

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:58.880
— meaning he talked about the movie as a
fictional character being played by another

00:01:58.880 --> 00:01:59.990
fictional character.

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:04.380
To sum it up, those who listen to the track
will hear Downey pretending to be an Australian

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:08.840
guy...pretending to be a black guy...talking
about a film… within a film.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.060
"Whoa!"

00:02:11.069 --> 00:02:12.640
What Danny don't do

00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:16.120
Everyone who's seen Machete knows one thing
for sure:

00:02:16.120 --> 00:02:18.110
"Machete don't text."

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:22.700
What you probably didn't know is that this
line came about because star Danny Trejo also

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:23.950
doesn't text.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:28.129
Instead, he tried to call director Robert
Rodriguez multiple times to discuss some ideas

00:02:28.129 --> 00:02:29.620
about Machete's character.

00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:34.200
Rodriguez finally called back and asked why
on Earth Trejo didn't just text him.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:38.270
Trejo's response was to get in character and
growl the since-immortalized line.

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:42.010
Rodriguez laughed so hard he ended up putting
it in the film.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.230
Liam Neeson has a particular set of skills

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:50.220
Bryan Mills, Liam Neeson's character from
the Taken franchise, can end a human life

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.640
with nothing more than a pinpoint-accurate
slap to the throat.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:56.220
In other words, he's a pretty scary guy.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:59.791
"But what I do are a very particular set of
skills.

00:03:00.520 --> 00:03:04.420
Skills I have acquired over a very long career.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.700
Skills that make me a nightmare for people
like you."

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:11.560
So imagine how terrified an unnamed ex-boyfriend
of Maggie Grace, who plays Mills' daughter

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:15.890
throughout the series, must have been when
Neeson, in character as Mills, called him

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:18.270
up to threaten to punch his arms off.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:20.260
As a joke, of course.

00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.950
Ha ha?

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:24.650
Adam Driver does not need a hug

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:27.890
According to pretty much everyone involved
with the production of Star Wars: The Force

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:32.790
Awakens, Adam Driver spent almost all of his
time on the set in character as the sullen

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:33.790
Kylo Ren.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:37.329
He was so emo, his co-stars felt compelled
to try to cheer him up.

00:03:37.329 --> 00:03:41.129
Mark Hamill, for instance, offered to take
Driver to lunch and repeatedly asked the young

00:03:41.129 --> 00:03:43.049
actor if he'd like to hang out.

00:03:43.049 --> 00:03:46.110
Not wanting to break character, Driver turned
him down.

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:50.819
John Boyega, on the other hand, took a more
direct approach, randomly hugging Driver without

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:53.739
warning in full costume throughout production.

00:03:53.739 --> 00:03:58.930
According to Boyega, Driver never once so
much as smirked; upon being hugged, he'd stand

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:02.830
awkwardly until Boyega was done before walking
away.

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.579
Game of Leers

00:04:04.579 --> 00:04:08.629
Everyone has their favorite Game of Thrones
characters, but two characters in particular

00:04:08.629 --> 00:04:13.599
have sparked fans' imaginations thanks to
their hilariously one-sided sexual tension:

00:04:13.599 --> 00:04:18.470
bearded wildling Tormund Giantsbane, played
by Kristofer Hivju, and the long-legged sentinel

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:22.550
of iron-plated justice Brienne of Tarth, played
by Gwendoline Christie.

00:04:22.550 --> 00:04:24.780
"I want to make babies with her.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.340
Think of them.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:27.900
Great, big monsters.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.540
They'd conquer the world."

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:34.170
Christie said that even she was taken aback
at the "magnitude of intense sexual intention"

00:04:34.170 --> 00:04:37.620
Hivju brought to the role, something he carried
over between takes.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:42.470
He reportedly attempted to woo her by sensually
eating a sandwich while maintaining unflinching

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:45.760
eye contact in full costume between takes.

00:04:45.760 --> 00:04:49.570
Which, to be fair, sounds exactly like something
Tormund would do.

00:04:49.570 --> 00:04:54.110
"Really kinda making love to that sandwich
as he eyeballs me."

00:04:54.110 --> 00:04:56.690
"Which is really strong, eyes like lasers."

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:59.310
Mrs. Doubtfire visited an adult shop

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:03.670
Mrs. Doubtfire is fondly remembered as one
of Robin Williams' most famous roles.

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:07.820
But before the film was announced, he decided
to see just how well the costume disguised

00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:12.820
his extremely famous face — by visiting
an adult shop in San Francisco.

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:17.110
Williams walked into the store in full Mrs.
Doubtfire gear and started browsing the various

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:21.940
items on display, asking an increasingly bemused
cashier the most uncomfortable questions he

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:25.210
could think of in Doubtfire's wonderful old
lady voice.

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:29.400
"And finally the guy realized it was me and
said, 'Get out of here, Robin, you ---hole!"

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.400
Thanks for watching!

